## Context
Audit after the 0116 merge surfaced 9 Go unit test coverage gaps and
fixture brittleness items. Several behaviours are exercised only via
shell tests; others have no fixture coverage at all.

## Missing Go unit tests
1. `staleBlockedBy` (check.go:33): closed-blocker detection has only
   shell-level coverage (`tests/test_check.sh:436`). Add Go unit test
   constructing two tickets and asserting the warning fires.
2. `pathIsClosed` (erg.go:58): path-component closure test exercised
   only indirectly via shell test_check.sh. Add Go unit test for the
   path-component cases (`closed/`, `closed-`, `closed.`, `-closed`).
3. `globLocalIDs` (validate.go:247): no Go unit test for the local-ID
   glob walker.

## Underspecified tests
4. Singleton "first occurrence wins" value preservation untested:
   `TestParseErg` only checks repeated `Blocked-by` count, not that
   `Title` keeps the first value when duplicated — erg_test.go:44.
5. Empty `Tag:` silently skipped (parser strips empty tags): untested.
   Add a fixture asserting `Tag: ` produces no Tag entry — erg.go:273.

## Fixture brittleness
6. `testdata/valid/0002-with-blockers.erg` references nonexistent
   blocker; only validates because `TestValidateErg_GoldenValid` builds
   `allIDs` from fixture filenames. Brittle to fixture rename.
7. No fixture for `Closed :` (whitespace before colon, which
   `parseHeaderLine` accepts but `isClosedHeaderLine` does not) —
   divergence between header parser and Closed-in-log/body detector.
   Add a fixture pinning the current behaviour, or fix the divergence.

## Coverage-set gaps
8. `ValidTagValues` closed set: only `needs-human` and `deferred`
   exercised as accept cases in Go tests. Add accept-cases for
   `post-talk` and `post-conference`.
9. `testdata/invalid/0001-missing-required.erg` omits only `Author`.
   No fixture omits `Title` or `Created`. Add two fixtures to close
   the golden-invalid coverage gap.

## Actions
1. Write Go unit tests for items 1-3 (use `testing.T` table-driven
   patterns; mirror the style of `TestParseErg`).
2. Extend existing tests for items 4-5.
3. Decide on items 6-7: either harden the fixture by giving it a real
   blocker, or document the brittleness explicitly. For item 7, decide
   whether to align parser and detector or pin the current divergence.
4. Add fixtures for items 8-9.

## Out of scope
- Defer-to-0117 items: duplicated required-header tests (Go + shell)
  and rule-numbering inconsistency — 0117 reorganizes validate.go.

## Exit criteria
- All 9 items addressed.
- `make test` passes; new tests fail on a regression (verify by
  temporarily breaking the relevant code, confirming the test catches
  it, then unbreaking).
